          "documents": [
            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Office Visit",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2026-01-27T08:40",
              "body": "Here for a routine follow-up and tells me he was in the ICU earlier this month. We heard nothing from the hospital.\n\nHis account, with his brother filling in: had switched from beer to vodka over the fall, about a pint a day. Decided to quit cold on his own around the 9th. Within a day and a half he was shaking, sweating, frightened; brother called 911. Spent most of a week in the hospital, several days in the ICU, \"out of my head\" for the first few. Told it was DTs. No seizure that he knows of. No new medicines at discharge.\n\nToday: calm, oriented, no tremor. HR 84. Weight 54.\nPHQ-9 7; low mood since, no SI.\n\nA/P\n1. Delirium tremens, 1/2026, by patient and family report; records requested. Added to problem list.\n2. Severe AUD: two withdrawal hospitalizations in ten weeks, now DTs. Told him directly that the next unsupervised stop could kill him. If he wants to quit again (he says he does), it has to be through a medically supervised detox; gave the program number and said I would call with him. He said not today. Brother on board.\n3. Labs today.\nRTC 4 weeks."
            }
          ]
