            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Post-hospital Visit",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2026-07-28T08:50",
              "body": "Discharge summary (7/14-7/20) reviewed: pneumonia, then two withdrawal seizures on day 2. CT head negative.\n\nHe feels tired but better. Cough mostly gone, no fever, breathing fine. No further seizures; doesn't remember them. Has not had a drink since admission, about two weeks; brother confirms. Not driving.\n\nExam: afebrile, RR and SpO2 normal. Lungs with good air movement, clear today. Heart regular. Calm, no tremor. Wide-based gait at baseline.\n\nA/P\n1. CAP: clinically resolving. Repeat 2-view CXR in early to mid September per the hospital; ordered.\n2. Alcohol withdrawal seizures: single episode in hospital, no recurrence. No driving per state rules for now; discussed.\n3. Severe AUD: withdrawal seizures now on top of DTs in January. Very direct conversation. He says he's \"really done\" this time. Gave the supervised program number again and offered to call together; he asked for a week to think.\n4. Labs today.\nRTC mid-September after the x-ray."
